      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im seeing this weird 500 error on our /api/v1/checkout endpoint sometimes. it happens randomly during peak traffic but i cant replicate it in staging. here is the log snippet from the last crash:\n\nError: Internal Server Error\nat RequestHandler (/app/src/middleware/auth.js:42:11)\nat processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:95:5)\nUnhandledPromiseRejectionWarning: Timeout error connecting to redis_cache_cluster at 10.0.2.15:6379\n{ status: 500, code: 'ECONNRESET', detail: 'connection lost' }\n\nany idea what would cause this to be intermittent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Intermittent 500s like that are usually a symptom of a downstream resource timing‑out – in your case the Redis cache. During peak traffic the connection pool can become exhausted, causing new requests to hit a timeout and bubble up as an `ECONNRESET`. Check that your Redis client’s pool size, retry logic, and socket timeouts are sized for load, and add back‑off/retry handling in the auth middleware so a single failed lookup doesn’t crash the whole request. Also monitor Redis latency and CPU during spikes; if the server is throttling you may need to scale the cluster or enable read replicas. Finally, wrap async calls in try/catch (or use `process.on('unhandledRejection')`) so the promise rejection is handled and logged instead of taking down the request thread.",
      "source": "target",
